WebAssembly build fixes for GNU APL svn trunk (verified at r2130).

1) libapl.cc fix_function_NL(): wrap Quad_FX::do_quad_FX() in try/catch like
   apl_exec() already is upstream. Redefining a native or locked function
   raises DEFN ERROR, which otherwise escapes across extern "C" as an
   uncaught C++ exception and kills the embedding host.
2) libapl.cc fix_function_NL(): do_quad_FX() never returns TOK_ERROR; a
   failed fix returns the error line as an integer scalar, a successful one
   the function name. Since do_quad_FX() fixes quietly (Bugs27 #59(i)),
   every bad definition was therefore reported as success, with no output.
   An integer scalar now raises DEFN ERROR, whose )MORE text UserFunction::
   fix() has already written.
3) libapl.cc: the private Quad_FX redeclaration gains the honor_lock
   parameter the real Quad_FX::do_quad_FX() now has, or it does not link.
4) UCS_string.cc operator<<: when the string is at least as wide as the
   stream's width, the width was left set and padded the first character
   instead. )HELP shows it wherever a command wider than the left column
   lands there (]FILE_CTL, ]KEYB).

patches/wasm-stubs.c (linked, not patched): sem_timedwait() returning ENOSYS,
referenced by Quad_PLOT.cc; a browser has no plot windows to wait for.

